  "nl_text": "The database name is rschema_0508, and it contains five tables: Member, Book, Order, Order_book, and Place_order. The Member table has the following columns: Address, Consumption_amount, Member_ID (primary key), Name, Password, Phone, Points, Postal_code, and Username. The Book table has the following columns: Author, Book_ID (primary key), Book_title, Category_name, ISBN, Price, Publication_date, and Publisher. The Order table has the following columns: Member_ID (foreign key referencing Member), Order_ID (primary key), Order_date, Sales_amount, Shipping_date, and a foreign key referencing Member. The Order_book table has the following columns: Book_ID (foreign key referencing Book), Order_ID (foreign key referencing Order), Quantity, and a composite primary key consisting of Order_ID and Book_ID. The Place_order table has the following columns: Member_ID (foreign key referencing Member), Order_ID (foreign key referencing Order), and a composite primary key consisting of Member_ID and Order_ID. The foreign keys in the Order_book and Place_order tables reference the primary keys in the Book and Order tables, respectively.",
  "gold_question": "This is an online bookstore backend database system. For member management, the system records basic information for each member, including unique member ID, username, password, name, address, postal code, phone number, consumption amount and points. For book management, the system records basic information for each book, including unique book ID, category name, book title, author, publisher, publication date, ISBN and price. For order management, the system records basic information for each order, including unique order ID, member username, sales amount, order date and shipping date. Each order can contain multiple books, and the system needs to record the purchase quantity for each book.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0508.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0508\nCREATE TABLE `member` (\n  `member_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `postal_code` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `points` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `consumption_amount` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`member_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `book` (\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `book_title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `author` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `publisher` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `isbn` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `price` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `publication_date` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  `category_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`book_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `order` (\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `member_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `order_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `shipping_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `sales_amount` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`order_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `order_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`member_id`) REFERENCES `member` (`member_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `order_book` (\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`order_id`, `book_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `order_book_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`order_id`) REFERENCES `order` (`order_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `order_book_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`book_id`) REFERENCES `book` (`book_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `place_order` (\n  `member_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`member_id`, `order_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `place_order_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`member_id`) REFERENCES `member` (`member_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `place_order_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`order_id`) REFERENCES `order` (`order_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
